    "_postman_id": "5debe50b-f7f2-4131-8b01-0394d4193811",
    "name": "Reqres API Testing",
    "description": "# Reqres API Testing\n\nThis collection contains automated API tests for user management and authentication flows using Reqres public API.\n\nThe purpose of this collection is to validate request-response behavior, authentication handling, and response structure validation.\n\nTest scenarios include:\n\n- User retrieval (list & single user)\n    \n- Create, update, and delete user\n    \n- Authentication (positive & negative cases)\n    \n\nbaseUrl using :\n\n[<code>https://reqres.in</code>](https://reqres.in)\n\nAll endpoints are prefix with:\n\n`/api`\n\nExample:\n\n`{{baseUrl}}/api/users/2`\n\n## **Authentication Method:**\n\nAll request under `/api` require the following header:\n\n`x-api-key :`\n\nThe API key is obtained from Reqres dashboard after you login to the app:\n\n[https://app.reqres.in/](https://app.reqres.in/)\n\n### Important Notes:\n\n- The API does **not validate Bearer tokens**.\n    \n- Sending a valid or invalid `Authorization: Bearer` header does not affect the response.\n    \n- As long as the correct `x-api-key` is provided, the API will return a successful response (200/201).\n    \n- If the `x-api-key` is missing or invalid, the API returns `401 Unauthorized`.\n    \n\nif request is under `/app` , then you can use bearer token.\n\n## **Test Coverage:**\n\n### 1 Status Code Validation\n\n- 200 OK\n    \n- 201 Created\n    \n- 400 Bad Request\n    \n\n### 2 Response Structure Validation\n\n- Required fields exist\n    \n- Data type validation\n    \n- Error message validation\n    \n\n### 3 Authentication Flow\n\n- Token generation\n    \n- Token storage in environment\n    \n- Negative login scenario\n    \n\n### 4 Data Integrity\n\n- User object contains required properties:\n    \n    - id\n        \n    - email\n        \n    - first_name\n        \n    - last_name\n        \n\n## Mock API Limitation\n\nThis API is a mock service provided by Reqres.  \n  \nIt does not persist created, updated, or deleted data.\n\nAll POST, PUT, and DELETE requests return simulated responses and do not modify the backend dataset.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- Created IDs cannot be retrieved afterward\n    \n- Update operations do not permanently change data\n    \n- Delete operations do not actually remove records\n    \n\nThe test scenarios are designed to validate response structure, status codes, and API behavior simulation only.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "52271318"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (positive)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {\r",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);\r",
                  "});\r",
                  "\r",
                  "const response = pm.response.json();\r",
                  "\r",
                  "pm.test(\"Token is exist\", function () {\r",
                  "    pm.expect(response.token).to.not.be.undefined;\r",
                  "});\r",
                  "\r",
                  "pm.environment.set(\"authtoken\", response.token);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-api-key",
                "value": "{{API_Key}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\r\n  \"email\": \"eve.holt@reqres.in\",\r\n  \"password\": \"cityslicka\"\r\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "login"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (negative)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 400\", function () {\r",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);\r",
                  "});\r",
                  "\r",
                  "const response = pm.response.json();\r",
                  "\r",
                  "pm.test(\"Error field is exist\", function () {\r",
                  "    pm.expect(response).to.have.property(\"error\"); \r",
                  "});\r",
                  "\r",
                  "pm.test(\"Error message is correct\", function () {\r",
                  "    pm.expect(response.error).to.eql(\"Missing email or username\"); \r",
                  "});\r",
                  "\r",
                  ""
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-api-key",
                "value": "{{API_Key}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\r\n  \"password\": \"cityslicka\"\r\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "login"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
